# LEA Professional Connect Series Amplifier Driver
#
# Controls LEA Connect Series smart amplifiers over the LEA Open API on TCP
# 4321. One driver covers the whole family: the Network Connect Series (analog
# inputs) and the Dante Connect Series ("D" models) speak the same API — LEA's
# protocol doc is explicit that it "outlines the TCP Protocol including commands
# that are available for all Dante Connect Series and Network Connect Series
# models". The differences are which values an element accepts, not which
# elements exist:
#   - Dante models add the "Dante 1".."Dante 7+8" input sources (all 8 Dante
#     inputs are available on every Dante model) and the Dante On Ramp control.
#   - Network Connect models expose only analog sources, and only as many as the
#     amp has channels (a 354 has no Analog 5-8).
# Selecting a source the amp doesn't have is benign: current firmware silently
# ignores it — no error, no change (verified on a Connect 352D running firmware
# 3.1.7.0). The source picker only offers valid values, so this is reachable only
# from a macro/script, and it fails silently rather than surfacing in last_error.
# (The 2020 protocol doc shows an "error: unsupported value: ..." reply here; that
# behavior is gone on current firmware — a bad enum value is now dropped silently.)
#
# Protocol reference: LEA Open API - TCP Protocol, Rev 2 (2020-10-02).
# Archived: driver-roadmap/reference-docs/lea-open-api-tcp-protocol.pdf
#
# Wire format:
#   Commands and responses are newline-delimited ('\n', 0x0a). A command with
#   no trailing newline gets NO response at all.
#     get <url>                -> "<url> <value>"
#     set <url> <value>        -> (no reply on success — controls only; a
#                                 subscribed element instead emits a change notice)
#     subscribe <url>          -> "<url> <value>", then a fresh line on
#                                 every change, on this same connection
#     unsubscribe <url>        -> "OK"
#   Verbs are case-insensitive; element URLs are case-sensitive. (The 2020 doc
#   says set answers "OK"; firmware 3.1.7.0 is silent on a successful set — the
#   only reply is the subscription notice, so the driver never waits on an ack.)
#   Values: strings and enums come back double-quoted ("Post Crossover");
#   booleans as bare true/false; every number is a float, even conceptual ints
#   ("70.0", "2.0"), often at full precision (-52.78131103515625). String/enum
#   values containing spaces MUST be quoted on the way in. Out-of-range numbers
#   are CLAMPED, not rejected (set fader -1000 is accepted silently; a subscriber
#   then sees -80.0).
#
# Push, not polling (Principle 2): every element the amp exposes is
# subscribable, and notifications arrive on the established control connection —
# so there is no `push:` block (that's for channels the platform must open).
# on_connect subscribes to the full surface; the subscribe reply doubles as the
# initial state sync, so the device is fully populated before the first poll.
#
# Level meters are opt-in (Enable Level Meters, default off). The amp pushes
# meter elements on change, not as a fixed-rate stream — measured at ~1.3 Hz per
# meter under signal, and effectively silent at idle, on a Connect 352D (firmware
# 3.1.7.0). An 8-channel unit with every meter subscribed is still ~40 streams,
# so meters stay opt-in for racks of amps, but the per-meter rate is modest. The
# meter subscriptions carry `when: enable_meters`; their response rules are
# throttled (~2 Hz, just above the measured push rate so nothing real is dropped)
# and their state vars are cloud_priority: low. With meters off, output level /
# volts / watts still refresh from the poll loop at poll_interval, which is the
# right cadence for amp telemetry (watts, impedance) as opposed to a live meter.
#
# Model naming decodes as <power per channel><channel count>[D]: a 704D is
# 700 W x 4 channels with Dante; a 168 is 160 W x 8 channels, analog only. Set
# Channels to that last digit (2, 4, or 8) — the amp reports its own count in
# num_outputs, so a mismatch is visible on the device card.

id: lea_connect
name: LEA Connect Series Amplifier
manufacturer: LEA Professional
category: audio
version: 1.0.0
author: OpenAVC
transport: tcp
delimiter: "\n"
min_platform_version: "0.23.0"

description: >
  Controls LEA Professional Connect Series smart amplifiers (Network Connect and
  Dante Connect) over the LEA Open API on TCP 4321. Each amplifier channel is a
  child entity with output mute, gain, Hi-Z/Lo-Z mode, input source selection
  with backup/override, crossover, RMS and peak limiters, load monitoring, and
  live meters. Amp-wide auto-standby, signal generator, power-supply monitoring,
  and fault reporting. State is push-driven: the driver subscribes to every
  element and the amp reports changes as they happen, including changes made
  from its own web UI.

source_url: https://leaprofessional.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/LEA-Open-API-TCP-Protocol-October-2020.pdf
tags: [amplifier, dsp, dante, power-amplifier, lea, connect-series, 70v, 100v]
verified: true
simulated: true
protocols: [lea_open_api]
ports: [4321]

compatible_models:
  - manufacturer: LEA Professional
    models:
      - Connect Series 352
      - Connect Series 702
      - Connect Series 124
      - Connect Series 164
      - Connect Series 354
      - Connect Series 704
      - Connect Series 1504
      - Connect Series 3004
      - Connect Series 84
      - Connect Series 88
      - Connect Series 168
    confidence: untested
    notes: >
      Network Connect Series (analog inputs, no Dante). The last digit of the
      model number is the channel count (352 = 2 channels, 704 = 4, 168 = 8).
      Analog sources are limited to the number of channels on the amp.
  - manufacturer: LEA Professional
    models:
      - Connect Series 352D
    confidence: full
    notes: >
      Verified end-to-end on real hardware — a Connect 352D on firmware 3.1.7.0
      (protocol, discovery, and control all confirmed). Same API as the rest of
      the Dante Connect Series below.
  - manufacturer: LEA Professional
    models:
      - Connect Series 702D
      - Connect Series 124D
      - Connect Series 164D
      - Connect Series 354D
      - Connect Series 704D
      - Connect Series 1504D
      - Connect Series 3004D
      - Connect Series 84D
      - Connect Series 88D
      - Connect Series 168D
    confidence: untested
    notes: >
      Dante Connect Series. Same API as the verified 352D; adds the eight Dante
      input sources (all eight are available on every Dante model regardless of
      channel count) and the Dante On Ramp control. Requires firmware 1.1.0.x or
      later — earlier firmware supports only the WebSocket API, not this TCP one.

help:
  overview: >
    LEA Connect Series amplifiers combine amplification with a full channel DSP:
    input selection with automatic backup/override, crossover, 8-band output EQ,
    RMS and peak limiters, and load monitoring on every channel. This driver
    exposes each amplifier channel as its own entity, so a panel can bind
    directly to "channel 3 mute" or "channel 1 output level" and macros can act
    on one channel without touching the others.

    The amp pushes changes as they happen, so the panel stays right even when
    someone changes something from the amplifier's own web UI or its front
    panel. Faults (channel fault, thermal, power supply, load short/open) arrive
    the moment they occur rather than on the next poll.
  setup: >
    1. Give the amplifier a static IP (or a DHCP reservation) — the amp's web UI
       or the LEA Cloud app both do this.
    2. Enter the IP here. The control port is 4321 and needs no username or
       password; the amp accepts control commands on it directly.
    3. That's it for channels — the amp reports its own channel count, so the
       roster fills in automatically once it connects (a 352 shows 2 channels, a
       704 shows 4). The "Channels" setting is only a fallback for building a
       project offline before the amp is reachable; set it to your model's count
       (the last digit of the model number) if you're working without the amp.
    4. Leave Enable Level Meters off unless you want live audio metering on a
       panel. Those per-channel level meters push while enabled; with meters off
       they refresh on the poll instead. (Power readings — AC voltage, current,
       watts — always push live regardless of this setting.)
    5. Firmware must be 1.1.0.x or newer. Older firmware only speaks the
       WebSocket API, which this driver does not use.

default_config:
  host: ""
  port: 4321
  poll_interval: 60
  inter_command_delay: 0.01
  channel_count: 4
  enable_meters: false
  tcp_keepalive: true

config_schema:
  host:
    type: string
    required: true
    default: ""
    label: "IP Address"
    description: "Amplifier IP address or hostname"
  port:
    type: integer
    required: true
    default: 4321
    label: "Port"
    description: "LEA Open API TCP port (fixed at 4321 on the amplifier)"
    min: 1
    max: 65535
  channel_count:
    type: enum
    required: false
    default: "4"
    label: "Channels (offline fallback)"
    description: "Fallback channel count for building the roster before the amp connects — once connected, the amp reports its real count and the roster auto-corrects. Set to your model's channel count for offline editing (the last digit of the model number: 704D = 4, 352 = 2, 168 = 8)."
    values:
      - { value: "2", label: "2 channels (352, 702)" }
      - { value: "4", label: "4 channels (124, 164, 354, 704, 1504, 3004, 84)" }
      - { value: "8", label: "8 channels (88, 168)" }
  enable_meters:
    type: boolean
    default: false
    label: "Enable Level Meters"
    description: >
      Subscribe to live meter streams (output level/volts/watts, input levels,
      limiter gain reduction). The amplifier streams these continuously, so this
      adds significant network traffic. With it off, output levels still refresh
      once per poll interval.
  poll_interval:
    type: integer
    default: 60
    label: "Poll Interval (s)"
    description: "State is pushed by the amp; this poll is a periodic re-sync and the meter refresh when meters are off."
    min: 0
    max: 3600

discovery:
  # Active fingerprint: the LEA Open API answers a modelID GET on 4321 with a
  # line no other protocol emits, and the value names the family outright
  # ("Connect Series Model 704D"). The tcp_probe is the primary identifier and
  # was confirmed against real hardware (a Connect 352D answered the probe on a
  # live scan, matching IDENTIFIED via the catalog).
  tcp_probe:
    port: 4321
    send_ascii: "get /amp/deviceInfo/modelID\n"
    expect_regex: '/amp/deviceInfo/modelID "Connect Series'
    extract_manufacturer: "LEA Professional"
    timeout_ms: 2000
  # OUI read off real hardware (Connect 352D MAC 64:8c:bb:f2:12:f1). LEA publishes
  # no MAC prefix, so this was not declared until an amp was on the bench. It is a
  # corroborating signal / vendor-name source; the tcp_probe above does the
  # identifying.
  oui:
    - "64:8c:bb"
  port_open:
    - 4321
  manufacturer_alias:
    - "lea"
    - "lea professional"

child_entity_types:
  channel:
    label: "Channel"
    label_plural: "Channels"
    id_format:
      type: integer
      min: 1
      max: 8
      pad_width: 2
    instances:
      # The amp reports its own channel count as num_outputs, so the roster
      # tracks the hardware — a 352 comes up as 2 channels, a 704 as 4, with no
      # manual step. channel_count is only the offline fallback (before the amp
      # has reported), so a project built without the amp still shows a roster.
      count_from_state: num_outputs
      count_from: channel_count
      label: "Channel {id}"
    label_field: name
    summary_fields: ["name", "mute", "fader", "output_signal_detect", "fault"]
    state_variables:
      # ── Output ──
      name:
        type: string
        label: "Channel Name"
        help: "The name given to this output channel on the amplifier"
      enable:
        type: boolean
        label: "Channel Ready Enable"
        help: "Whether the channel is armed to pass audio"
        cloud_priority: high
      mute:
        type: boolean
        label: "Mute"
        control: true
        cloud_priority: high
      fader:
        type: number
        label: "Output Level (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        step: 0.5
        unit: "dB"
        control: true
        cloud_priority: high
      hiz_loz:
        type: enum
        values: ["HiZ-70V", "HiZ-100V", "LoZ"]
        label: "Output Mode"
        help: "70 V / 100 V constant-voltage, or low-impedance"
      hiz_hpf_frequency:
        type: integer
        label: "Hi-Z High Pass (Hz)"
        min: 35
        max: 5000
        unit: "Hz"
      fault:
        type: boolean
        label: "Fault"
        help: "Channel shut down by protection — check for a shorted output"
        cloud_priority: high
      thermal:
        type: boolean
        label: "Thermal Fault"
        cloud_priority: high
      limiting:
        type: boolean
        label: "Limiting"
        cloud_priority: high
      output_clip:
        type: boolean
        label: "Output Clip"
        cloud_priority: high
      output_signal_detect:
        type: boolean
        label: "Output Signal Present"
        cloud_priority: high
      ready:
        type: boolean
        label: "Ready"
        help: "Channel is ready to pass audio"
        cloud_priority: high

      # ── Meters (streamed only while Enable Level Meters is on) ──
      level_db:
        type: number
        label: "Output Level (dBFS)"
        min: -60.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dBFS"
        cloud_priority: low
      level_volts:
        type: number
        label: "Output (V RMS)"
        min: 0.0
        max: 200.0
        unit: "V"
        cloud_priority: low
      level_watts:
        type: number
        label: "Output (W RMS)"
        min: 0.0
        max: 10000.0
        unit: "W"
        cloud_priority: low

      # ── Input selector ──
      primary_source:
        type: string
        label: "Primary Source"
        help: "Analog or Dante input feeding this channel"
        control: true
        cloud_priority: high
      primary_fader:
        type: number
        label: "Primary Input Level (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        step: 0.5
        unit: "dB"
        control: true
      primary_level:
        type: number
        label: "Primary Input Meter (dBFS)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dBFS"
        cloud_priority: low
      primary_signal_detect:
        type: boolean
        label: "Primary Signal Present"
      primary_clip:
        type: boolean
        label: "Primary Input Clip"
      primary_threshold:
        type: number
        label: "Primary Override Threshold (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      secondary_source:
        type: string
        label: "Secondary Source"
        help: "Backup / override source, or None"
      secondary_fader:
        type: number
        label: "Secondary Input Level (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        step: 0.5
        unit: "dB"
      secondary_level:
        type: number
        label: "Secondary Input Meter (dBFS)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dBFS"
        cloud_priority: low
      secondary_signal_detect:
        type: boolean
        label: "Secondary Signal Present"
      secondary_clip:
        type: boolean
        label: "Secondary Input Clip"
      secondary_threshold:
        type: number
        label: "Secondary Override Threshold (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
      input_signal_detect:
        type: boolean
        label: "Input Signal Present"
        help: "Aggregate of the primary and secondary inputs"
        cloud_priority: high
      input_clip:
        type: boolean
        label: "Input Clip"
        help: "Aggregate of the primary and secondary inputs"
      input_mode:
        type: enum
        values: ["Override", "Backup"]
        label: "Priority Mode"
        help: "Override = auto-override the primary input; Backup = signal-sensing override"
      signal_gen_enable:
        type: boolean
        label: "Signal Generator On"
      signal_gen_fader:
        type: number
        label: "Signal Generator Level (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        step: 0.5
        unit: "dB"
      dante_on_ramp:
        type: string
        label: "Dante On Ramp"
        help: "Dante models only — what this channel puts onto the Dante network"

      # ── Crossover ──
      xover_gain:
        type: number
        label: "Crossover Gain (dB)"
        min: -15.0
        max: 15.0
        step: 0.5
        unit: "dB"
      xover_delay:
        type: number
        label: "Output Delay (ms)"
        min: 0.0
        max: 100.0
        unit: "ms"
      xover_invert:
        type: boolean
        label: "Polarity Invert"
      lpf_enable:
        type: boolean
        label: "Low Pass Filter On"
      lpf_type:
        type: string
        label: "Low Pass Filter Type"
      lpf_frequency:
        type: integer
        label: "Low Pass Frequency (Hz)"
        min: 20
        max: 20000
        unit: "Hz"
      hpf_enable:
        type: boolean
        label: "High Pass Filter On"
      hpf_type:
        type: string
        label: "High Pass Filter Type"
      hpf_frequency:
        type: integer
        label: "High Pass Frequency (Hz)"
        min: 20
        max: 20000
        unit: "Hz"

      # ── RMS limiter ──
      rms_enable:
        type: boolean
        label: "RMS Limiter On"
      rms_threshold:
        type: number
        label: "RMS Limiter Threshold (V)"
        min: 10.0
        max: 140.0
        unit: "V"
      rms_attack:
        type: number
        label: "RMS Limiter Attack (ms)"
        min: 1000.0
        max: 10000.0
        unit: "ms"
      rms_release:
        type: number
        label: "RMS Limiter Release (ms)"
        min: 1000.0
        max: 10000.0
        unit: "ms"
      rms_gain_reduction:
        type: number
        label: "RMS Speaker Limiter Reduction (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
        cloud_priority: low
      rms_total_gain_reduction:
        type: number
        label: "RMS Total Limiter Reduction (dB)"
        help: "Includes the amplifier's own protection limiters"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
        cloud_priority: low

      # ── Peak limiter ──
      peak_enable:
        type: boolean
        label: "Peak Limiter On"
      peak_threshold:
        type: number
        label: "Peak Limiter Threshold (V)"
        min: 14.0
        max: 198.0
        unit: "V"
      peak_attack:
        type: number
        label: "Peak Limiter Attack (ms)"
        min: 1.0
        max: 1000.0
        unit: "ms"
      peak_release:
        type: number
        label: "Peak Limiter Release (ms)"
        min: 1.0
        max: 1000.0
        unit: "ms"
      peak_gain_reduction:
        type: number
        label: "Peak Speaker Limiter Reduction (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
        cloud_priority: low
      peak_total_gain_reduction:
        type: number
        label: "Peak Total Limiter Reduction (dB)"
        help: "Includes the amplifier's own protection limiters"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        unit: "dB"
        cloud_priority: low

      # ── Load monitoring ──
      load_monitor_enable:
        type: boolean
        label: "Load Monitor On"
      impedance:
        type: number
        label: "Measured Impedance (ohm)"
        min: 0.0
        max: 250.0
        unit: "ohm"
        cloud_priority: low
      load_high_limit:
        type: number
        label: "Load High Limit (ohm)"
        min: 8.0
        max: 250.0
        unit: "ohm"
      load_low_limit:
        type: number
        label: "Load Low Limit (ohm)"
        min: 1.0
        max: 250.0
        unit: "ohm"
      load_status:
        type: enum
        values: ["Ok", "Short", "Open", "Low Signal"]
        label: "Load Status"
        help: "Ok = measured impedance is between the low and high limits"
        cloud_priority: high

  analog_input:
    label: "Analog Input"
    label_plural: "Analog Inputs"
    id_format:
      type: integer
      min: 1
      max: 8
      pad_width: 2
    instances:
      # The amp has as many analog inputs as it has channels (LEA: analog inputs
      # are "only available for the number of inputs on the amplifier"). Dante
      # models add eight Dante inputs, which are sources rather than physical
      # inputs and carry no per-input settings. The amp reports its analog input
      # count as num_inputs, so the roster follows that; channel_count is the
      # offline fallback (before the amp has reported).
      count_from_state: num_inputs
      count_from: channel_count
      label: "Analog Input {id}"
    summary_fields: ["sensitivity"]
    state_variables:
      sensitivity:
        type: enum
        values: ["26dB", "34dB"]
        label: "Input Sensitivity"
        help: "26 dB for consumer/line level, 34 dB for professional line level"

state_variables:
  # ── Identity ──
  device_name:
    type: string
    label: "Device Name"
  venue_name:
    type: string
    label: "Venue Name"
  model_id:
    type: string
    label: "Model"
  serial_number:
    type: string
    label: "Serial Number"
  asset_tag:
    type: string
    label: "Asset Tag"
  installer_name:
    type: string
    label: "Installer Name"
  installer_contact:
    type: string
    label: "Installer Contact"
  date_of_installation:
    type: string
    label: "Date of Installation"
  rack_name:
    type: string
    label: "Rack Name"
  rack_position:
    type: string
    label: "Rack Position"
  date_of_mfg:
    type: string
    label: "Date of Manufacture"
  hardware_id:
    type: string
    label: "Hardware ID"
  firmware_version:
    type: string
    label: "Firmware Version"
  psu_firmware_version:
    type: string
    label: "Power Supply Firmware"
  amp12_firmware_version:
    type: string
    label: "Amp 1/2 Firmware"
  amp34_firmware_version:
    type: string
    label: "Amp 3/4 Firmware"
  uptime:
    type: string
    label: "Up Time"
  num_inputs:
    type: integer
    label: "Num Inputs"
  num_outputs:
    type: integer
    label: "Num Outputs"
    help: "Channel count as the amplifier reports it — if this disagrees with the Channels setting, fix the setting"

  # ── Power supply ──
  ac_line_voltage:
    type: number
    label: "AC Line Voltage"
    min: 0.0
    max: 300.0
    unit: "V"
    cloud_priority: low
  ac_line_current:
    type: number
    label: "AC Line Current"
    min: 0.0
    max: 100.0
    unit: "A"
    cloud_priority: low
  ac_line_watts:
    type: number
    label: "AC Power Draw"
    min: 0.0
    max: 5000.0
    unit: "W"
    cloud_priority: low
  psu_fault:
    type: boolean
    label: "Power Supply Fault"
    cloud_priority: high
  psu_thermal:
    type: boolean
    label: "Power Supply Thermal"
    cloud_priority: high
  psu_power_ok:
    type: boolean
    label: "Power OK"
    cloud_priority: high
  psu_line_warning:
    type: boolean
    label: "AC Line Voltage OK"
    cloud_priority: high

  # ── Auto standby / signal generator ──
  auto_standby_enable:
    type: boolean
    label: "Auto Standby"
    control: true
  auto_standby_threshold:
    type: number
    label: "Auto Standby Threshold (dBFS)"
    min: -80.0
    max: 0.0
    unit: "dBFS"
  auto_standby_wait:
    type: integer
    label: "Auto Standby Wait (min)"
    min: 1
    max: 240
    unit: "min"
  signal_gen_type:
    type: enum
    values: ["Pink Noise", "White Noise", "Tone"]
    label: "Signal Generator Type"
  signal_gen_frequency:
    type: integer
    label: "Signal Generator Tone (Hz)"
    min: 20
    max: 20000
    unit: "Hz"

  last_error:
    type: string
    label: "Last Error"
    help: "Most recent error the amplifier returned (e.g. a malformed command or an unknown element)"

device_settings:
  # Amp-wide values the amplifier itself persists. Per-channel values (mute,
  # gain, crossover, limiters) are child state + child_id commands instead — a
  # device setting's state_key is flat and can't address a channel.
  #
  # The booleans here are declared `enum` on purpose: LEA takes a JSON boolean
  # on the wire (true / false, lowercase), and a `type: boolean` setting can
  # only render as {value} -> "True"/"False" or {value:d} -> "1"/"0", neither of
  # which the amp accepts. The backing state variables stay real booleans.
  device_name:
    type: string
    label: "Device Name"
    help: "Name shown for this amplifier in LEA Cloud and its web UI"
    default: ""
    state_key: "device_name"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: 'set /amp/deviceInfo/deviceName "{value}"\n'
  venue_name:
    type: string
    label: "Venue Name"
    default: ""
    state_key: "venue_name"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: 'set /amp/deviceInfo/venueName "{value}"\n'
  asset_tag:
    type: string
    label: "Asset Tag"
    default: ""
    state_key: "asset_tag"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: 'set /amp/deviceInfo/assetTagNumber "{value}"\n'
  installer_name:
    type: string
    label: "Installer Name"
    default: ""
    state_key: "installer_name"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: 'set /amp/deviceInfo/installerName "{value}"\n'
  installer_contact:
    type: string
    label: "Installer Contact"
    default: ""
    state_key: "installer_contact"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: 'set /amp/deviceInfo/installerContactInfo "{value}"\n'
  rack_name:
    type: string
    label: "Rack Name"
    default: ""
    state_key: "rack_name"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: 'set /amp/deviceInfo/rackName "{value}"\n'
  rack_position:
    type: string
    label: "Rack Position"
    default: ""
    state_key: "rack_position"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: 'set /amp/deviceInfo/rackPosition "{value}"\n'
  auto_standby_enable:
    type: enum
    values:
      - { value: "true", label: "On" }
      - { value: "false", label: "Off" }
    label: "Auto Standby"
    help: "Put the amplifier in standby after a period with no signal"
    default: "false"
    state_key: "auto_standby_enable"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "set /amp/autoStandby/enable {value}\n"
  auto_standby_threshold:
    type: number
    label: "Auto Standby Threshold (dBFS)"
    help: "Signal level below which the amp counts as idle"
    default: -60.0
    min: -80.0
    max: 0.0
    state_key: "auto_standby_threshold"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "set /amp/autoStandby/threshold {value}\n"
  auto_standby_wait:
    type: integer
    label: "Auto Standby Wait (min)"
    help: "Minutes of idle signal before the amp goes to standby"
    default: 15
    min: 1
    max: 240
    state_key: "auto_standby_wait"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "set /amp/autoStandby/timeToWait {value}\n"
  signal_gen_type:
    type: enum
    values: ["Pink Noise", "White Noise", "Tone"]
    label: "Signal Generator Type"
    default: "Pink Noise"
    state_key: "signal_gen_type"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: 'set /amp/signalGenerator/type "{value}"\n'
  signal_gen_frequency:
    type: integer
    label: "Signal Generator Tone (Hz)"
    default: 1000
    min: 20
    max: 20000
    state_key: "signal_gen_frequency"
    setup: false
    write:
      send: "set /amp/signalGenerator/frequency {value}\n"

commands:

  # ── Channel output ──

  mute_on:
    label: "Mute Channel"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/output/mute true\n"
    help: "Mute one amplifier channel"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"

  mute_off:
    label: "Unmute Channel"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/output/mute false\n"
    help: "Unmute one amplifier channel"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"

  set_fader:
    label: "Set Output Level"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/output/fader {level}\n"
    help: "Set a channel's output gain attenuation in dB (0 = unity, -80 = off)"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      level:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Level (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        decimals: 1

  set_channel_name:
    label: "Set Channel Name"
    send: 'set /amp/channels/{channel}/output/name "{name}"\n'
    help: "Name a channel on the amplifier (e.g. Bar Speakers)"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      name:
        type: string
        required: true
        label: "Name"

  channel_enable:
    label: "Enable Channel"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/output/enable true\n"
    help: "Arm a channel to pass audio"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"

  channel_disable:
    label: "Disable Channel"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/output/enable false\n"
    help: "Stop a channel passing audio"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"

  set_output_mode:
    label: "Set Output Mode"
    send: 'set /amp/channels/{channel}/output/hiZLoZ "{mode}"\n'
    help: "Constant-voltage (70 V / 100 V) or low-impedance output. Must match the speaker system on this channel."
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      mode:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Mode"
        values:
          - { value: "HiZ-70V", label: "Hi-Z 70 V" }
          - { value: "HiZ-100V", label: "Hi-Z 100 V" }
          - { value: "LoZ", label: "Low impedance" }

  set_hiz_hpf:
    label: "Set Hi-Z High Pass"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/output/hiZHpfFrequency {frequency}\n"
    help: "High-pass frequency applied in Hi-Z mode, protecting the distribution transformer"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      frequency:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: "Frequency (Hz)"
        min: 35
        max: 5000

  # ── Input selection ──

  set_primary_source:
    label: "Set Primary Source"
    send: 'set /amp/channels/{channel}/inputSelector/primary "{source}"\n'
    help: >
      Route an input to a channel. Analog sources beyond the amp's channel count
      and every Dante source exist only on the models that have them; picking one
      the amp doesn't have does nothing — current firmware silently ignores a
      source it can't honor (no error, no change), so double-check the model's
      real inputs.
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      source:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Source"
        values: &sources
          - "Analog 1"
          - "Analog 2"
          - "Analog 1+2"
          - "Analog 3"
          - "Analog 4"
          - "Analog 3+4"
          - "Analog 5"
          - "Analog 6"
          - "Analog 5+6"
          - "Analog 7"
          - "Analog 8"
          - "Analog 7+8"
          - "Dante 1"
          - "Dante 2"
          - "Dante 1+2"
          - "Dante 3"
          - "Dante 4"
          - "Dante 3+4"
          - "Dante 5"
          - "Dante 6"
          - "Dante 5+6"
          - "Dante 7"
          - "Dante 8"
          - "Dante 7+8"

  set_secondary_source:
    label: "Set Secondary Source"
    send: 'set /amp/channels/{channel}/inputSelector/secondary "{source}"\n'
    help: "Backup / override source for a channel, or None to disable it"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      source:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Source"
        values:
          - "None"
          - "Analog 1"
          - "Analog 2"
          - "Analog 1+2"
          - "Analog 3"
          - "Analog 4"
          - "Analog 3+4"
          - "Analog 5"
          - "Analog 6"
          - "Analog 5+6"
          - "Analog 7"
          - "Analog 8"
          - "Analog 7+8"
          - "Dante 1"
          - "Dante 2"
          - "Dante 1+2"
          - "Dante 3"
          - "Dante 4"
          - "Dante 3+4"
          - "Dante 5"
          - "Dante 6"
          - "Dante 5+6"
          - "Dante 7"
          - "Dante 8"
          - "Dante 7+8"

  set_primary_fader:
    label: "Set Primary Input Level"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/inputSelector/primaryFader {level}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      level:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Level (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        decimals: 1

  set_secondary_fader:
    label: "Set Secondary Input Level"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/inputSelector/secondaryFader {level}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      level:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Level (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        decimals: 1

  set_primary_threshold:
    label: "Set Primary Override Threshold"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/inputSelector/primaryThreshold {level}\n"
    help: "Signal level below which the primary input counts as absent"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      level:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Threshold (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        decimals: 1

  set_secondary_threshold:
    label: "Set Secondary Override Threshold"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/inputSelector/secondaryThreshold {level}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      level:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Threshold (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        decimals: 1

  set_input_mode:
    label: "Set Priority Mode"
    send: 'set /amp/channels/{channel}/inputSelector/mode "{mode}"\n'
    help: "Override = auto-override the primary input. Backup = switch on loss of signal."
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      mode:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Mode"
        values:
          - { value: "Override", label: "Auto override primary" }
          - { value: "Backup", label: "Signal-sensing backup" }

  set_input_sensitivity:
    label: "Set Analog Input Sensitivity"
    send: 'set /amp/inputs/analog/{input}/sensitivity "{sensitivity}"\n'
    help: "Input gain staging: 26 dB for consumer/line level, 34 dB for professional line level"
    params:
      input:
        type: child_id
        child_type: analog_input
        required: true
        label: "Analog Input"
      sensitivity:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Sensitivity"
        values: ["26dB", "34dB"]

  set_dante_on_ramp:
    label: "Set Dante On Ramp"
    send: 'set /amp/channels/{channel}/inputSelector/danteOnRamp "{tap}"\n'
    help: "Dante models only — where this channel's Dante transmit signal is tapped from"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      tap:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Tap Point"
        values: ["Analog Input", "Post Crossover"]

  # ── Signal generator ──

  signal_gen_on:
    label: "Signal Generator On"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/inputSelector/signalGeneratorEnable true\n"
    help: "Feed the amp-wide signal generator into one channel (for commissioning)"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"

  signal_gen_off:
    label: "Signal Generator Off"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/inputSelector/signalGeneratorEnable false\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"

  set_signal_gen_fader:
    label: "Set Signal Generator Level"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/inputSelector/signalGeneratorFader {level}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      level:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Level (dB)"
        min: -80.0
        max: 0.0
        decimals: 1

  # ── Crossover ──

  set_crossover_gain:
    label: "Set Crossover Gain"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/crossover/bandGainAndDelay/gain {gain}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      gain:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Gain (dB)"
        min: -15.0
        max: 15.0
        decimals: 1

  set_output_delay:
    label: "Set Output Delay"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/crossover/bandGainAndDelay/delay {delay}\n"
    help: "Time-align this channel's speakers with the rest of the system"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      delay:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Delay (ms)"
        min: 0.0
        max: 100.0
        decimals: 1

  set_polarity:
    label: "Set Polarity"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/crossover/bandGainAndDelay/invert {invert}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      invert:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Polarity"
        values:
          - { value: "false", label: "Normal (+)" }
          - { value: "true", label: "Inverted (-)" }

  set_low_pass:
    label: "Set Low Pass Filter"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/crossover/lowPassFilter/enable {enable}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      enable:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Low Pass Filter"
        values:
          - { value: "true", label: "On" }
          - { value: "false", label: "Off" }

  set_low_pass_type:
    label: "Set Low Pass Type"
    send: 'set /amp/channels/{channel}/crossover/lowPassFilter/type "{type}"\n'
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      type:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Filter Type"
        values: &filter_types
          - "Butterworth 6dB/oct"
          - "Butterworth 12dB/oct"
          - "Butterworth 18dB/oct"
          - "Butterworth 24dB/oct"
          - "Butterworth 48dB/oct"
          - "Linkwitz-Riley 24dB/oct"
          - "Linkwitz-Riley 48dB/oct"
          - "Bessel 6dB/oct"
          - "Bessel 12dB/oct"
          - "Bessel 18dB/oct"
          - "Bessel 24dB/oct"
          - "Bessel 48dB/oct"

  set_low_pass_frequency:
    label: "Set Low Pass Frequency"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/crossover/lowPassFilter/frequency {frequency}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      frequency:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: "Frequency (Hz)"
        min: 20
        max: 20000

  set_high_pass:
    label: "Set High Pass Filter"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/crossover/highPassFilter/enable {enable}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      enable:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "High Pass Filter"
        values:
          - { value: "true", label: "On" }
          - { value: "false", label: "Off" }

  set_high_pass_type:
    label: "Set High Pass Type"
    send: 'set /amp/channels/{channel}/crossover/highPassFilter/type "{type}"\n'
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      type:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Filter Type"
        values: *filter_types

  set_high_pass_frequency:
    label: "Set High Pass Frequency"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/crossover/highPassFilter/frequency {frequency}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      frequency:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: "Frequency (Hz)"
        min: 20
        max: 20000

  # ── Output EQ (8 bands per channel) ──
  # The EQ is a channel-of-filters, which the child-entity model can't nest, so
  # the filters are write-only commands rather than state. Nothing is faked: the
  # driver reports no EQ state rather than echoing back what it last sent.

  set_eq_enable:
    label: "Set EQ Band On/Off"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/outputEqFilters/{band}/enable {enable}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      band:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: "EQ Band"
        min: 1
        max: 8
      enable:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Band"
        values:
          - { value: "true", label: "On" }
          - { value: "false", label: "Off" }

  set_eq_type:
    label: "Set EQ Band Type"
    send: 'set /amp/channels/{channel}/outputEqFilters/{band}/type "{type}"\n'
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      band:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: "EQ Band"
        min: 1
        max: 8
      type:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Filter Type"
        values:
          - "Parametric"
          - "LP Shelf 6dB/oct"
          - "HP Shelf 6dB/oct"
          - "LP Shelf 12dB/oct"
          - "HP Shelf 12dB/oct"

  set_eq_gain:
    label: "Set EQ Band Gain"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/outputEqFilters/{band}/gain {gain}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      band:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: "EQ Band"
        min: 1
        max: 8
      gain:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Gain (dB)"
        min: -15.0
        max: 15.0
        decimals: 1

  set_eq_frequency:
    label: "Set EQ Band Frequency"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/outputEqFilters/{band}/frequency {frequency}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      band:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: "EQ Band"
        min: 1
        max: 8
      frequency:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: "Frequency (Hz)"
        min: 20
        max: 20000

  set_eq_q:
    label: "Set EQ Band Q"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/outputEqFilters/{band}/q {q}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      band:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: "EQ Band"
        min: 1
        max: 8
      q:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Q"
        min: 0.1
        max: 24.0
        decimals: 2

  # ── Limiters ──

  set_rms_limiter:
    label: "Set RMS Limiter"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/rmsLimiter/enable {enable}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      enable:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "RMS Limiter"
        values:
          - { value: "true", label: "On" }
          - { value: "false", label: "Off" }

  set_rms_threshold:
    label: "Set RMS Limiter Threshold"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/rmsLimiter/threshold {threshold}\n"
    help: "Speaker's continuous voltage rating"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      threshold:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Threshold (V)"
        min: 10.0
        max: 140.0
        decimals: 1

  set_rms_attack:
    label: "Set RMS Limiter Attack"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/rmsLimiter/attackTime {time}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      time:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Attack (ms)"
        min: 1000.0
        max: 10000.0
        decimals: 0

  set_rms_release:
    label: "Set RMS Limiter Release"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/rmsLimiter/releaseTime {time}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      time:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Release (ms)"
        min: 1000.0
        max: 10000.0
        decimals: 0

  set_peak_limiter:
    label: "Set Peak Limiter"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/peakLimiter/enable {enable}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      enable:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Peak Limiter"
        values:
          - { value: "true", label: "On" }
          - { value: "false", label: "Off" }

  set_peak_threshold:
    label: "Set Peak Limiter Threshold"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/peakLimiter/threshold {threshold}\n"
    help: "Speaker's peak voltage rating"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      threshold:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Threshold (V)"
        min: 14.0
        max: 198.0
        decimals: 1

  set_peak_attack:
    label: "Set Peak Limiter Attack"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/peakLimiter/attackTime {time}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      time:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Attack (ms)"
        min: 1.0
        max: 1000.0
        decimals: 1

  set_peak_release:
    label: "Set Peak Limiter Release"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/peakLimiter/releaseTime {time}\n"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      time:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Release (ms)"
        min: 1.0
        max: 1000.0
        decimals: 1

  # ── Load monitoring ──

  set_load_monitor:
    label: "Set Load Monitor"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/loadMonitor/enable {enable}\n"
    help: "Watch this channel's speaker load for a short or an open circuit"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      enable:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Load Monitor"
        values:
          - { value: "true", label: "On" }
          - { value: "false", label: "Off" }

  set_load_high_limit:
    label: "Set Load High Limit"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/loadMonitor/highLimit {limit}\n"
    help: "Impedance above this reads as an open circuit (a disconnected speaker)"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      limit:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "High Limit (ohm)"
        min: 8.0
        max: 250.0
        decimals: 1

  set_load_low_limit:
    label: "Set Load Low Limit"
    send: "set /amp/channels/{channel}/loadMonitor/lowLimit {limit}\n"
    help: "Impedance below this reads as a short circuit"
    params:
      channel:
        type: child_id
        child_type: channel
        required: true
        label: "Channel"
      limit:
        type: number
        required: true
        label: "Low Limit (ohm)"
        min: 1.0
        max: 250.0
        decimals: 1

  # ── Amp-wide ──

  set_auto_standby:
    label: "Set Auto Standby"
    send: "set /amp/autoStandby/enable {enable}\n"
    params:
      enable:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Auto Standby"
        values:
          - { value: "true", label: "On" }
          - { value: "false", label: "Off" }

  set_signal_gen_type:
    label: "Set Signal Generator Type"
    send: 'set /amp/signalGenerator/type "{type}"\n'
    params:
      type:
        type: enum
        required: true
        label: "Type"
        values: ["Pink Noise", "White Noise", "Tone"]

  set_signal_gen_frequency:
    label: "Set Signal Generator Tone"
    send: "set /amp/signalGenerator/frequency {frequency}\n"
    params:
      frequency:
        type: integer
        required: true
        label: "Frequency (Hz)"
        min: 20
        max: 20000

quick_actions: [mute_on, mute_off, set_fader, set_primary_source]

responses:
  # Every reply and every subscription notice has the same shape:
  #   <element url> <value>
  # so one rule per element routes both the initial subscribe reply and every
  # later change. Channel rules capture the channel number into the child id.
  # Order matters only where one pattern could shadow another; the URLs are
  # distinct, so these read in protocol order.

  # ── Channel: output ──
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/output/name "(.*)"$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { name: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/output/enable (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { enable: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/output/mute (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { mute: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/output/fader (-?[\d.]+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { fader: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/output/hiZLoZ "(.*)"$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { hiz_loz: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/output/hiZHpfFrequency (\d+)(?:\.\d+)?$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { hiz_hpf_frequency: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/output/fault (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { fault: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/output/thermal (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { thermal: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/output/limiting (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { limiting: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/output/clip (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { output_clip: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/output/signalDetect (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { output_signal_detect: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/output/ready (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { ready: $2 } }

  # ── Channel: meters (pushed on change — throttled to bound state writes) ──
  # throttle is scoped per routed child, so `throttle: 0.5` caps each channel at
  # 2 writes/sec independently (not divided across channels). 0.5 sits just above
  # the ~1.3 Hz the amp was measured to push per meter under signal, so a live
  # meter passes through untouched while a pathological burst is still capped.
  # Nothing that must not be missed (a fault, a mute) is a throttled meter.
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/levels/level_db (-?[\d.]+)$'
    throttle: 0.5
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { level_db: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/levels/level_volts (-?[\d.]+)$'
    throttle: 0.5
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { level_volts: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/levels/level_watts (-?[\d.]+)$'
    throttle: 0.5
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { level_watts: $2 } }

  # ── Channel: input selector ──
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/primary "(.*)"$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { primary_source: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/primaryFader (-?[\d.]+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { primary_fader: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/primaryLevel (-?[\d.]+)$'
    throttle: 0.5
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { primary_level: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/primarySignalDetect (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { primary_signal_detect: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/primaryClip (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { primary_clip: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/primaryThreshold (-?[\d.]+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { primary_threshold: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/secondary "(.*)"$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { secondary_source: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/secondaryFader (-?[\d.]+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { secondary_fader: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/secondaryLevel (-?[\d.]+)$'
    throttle: 0.5
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { secondary_level: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/secondarySignalDetect (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { secondary_signal_detect: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/secondaryClip (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { secondary_clip: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/secondaryThreshold (-?[\d.]+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { secondary_threshold: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/signalDetect (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { input_signal_detect: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/clip (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { input_clip: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/mode "(.*)"$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { input_mode: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/signalGeneratorEnable (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { signal_gen_enable: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/signalGeneratorFader (-?[\d.]+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { signal_gen_fader: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/inputSelector/danteOnRamp "(.*)"$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { dante_on_ramp: $2 } }

  # ── Channel: crossover ──
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/crossover/bandGainAndDelay/gain (-?[\d.]+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { xover_gain: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/crossover/bandGainAndDelay/delay (-?[\d.]+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { xover_delay: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/crossover/bandGainAndDelay/invert (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { xover_invert: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/crossover/lowPassFilter/enable (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { lpf_enable: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/crossover/lowPassFilter/type "(.*)"$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { lpf_type: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/crossover/lowPassFilter/frequency (\d+)(?:\.\d+)?$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { lpf_frequency: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/crossover/highPassFilter/enable (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { hpf_enable: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/crossover/highPassFilter/type "(.*)"$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { hpf_type: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/crossover/highPassFilter/frequency (\d+)(?:\.\d+)?$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { hpf_frequency: $2 } }

  # ── Channel: limiters ──
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/rmsLimiter/enable (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { rms_enable: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/rmsLimiter/threshold (-?[\d.]+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { rms_threshold: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/rmsLimiter/attackTime (-?[\d.]+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { rms_attack: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/rmsLimiter/releaseTime (-?[\d.]+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { rms_release: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/rmsLimiter/gainReduction (-?[\d.]+)$'
    throttle: 0.5
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { rms_gain_reduction: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/rmsLimiter/totalGainReduction (-?[\d.]+)$'
    throttle: 0.5
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { rms_total_gain_reduction: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/peakLimiter/enable (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { peak_enable: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/peakLimiter/threshold (-?[\d.]+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { peak_threshold: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/peakLimiter/attackTime (-?[\d.]+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { peak_attack: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/peakLimiter/releaseTime (-?[\d.]+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { peak_release: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/peakLimiter/gainReduction (-?[\d.]+)$'
    throttle: 0.5
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { peak_gain_reduction: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/peakLimiter/totalGainReduction (-?[\d.]+)$'
    throttle: 0.5
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { peak_total_gain_reduction: $2 } }

  # ── Channel: load monitor ──
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/loadMonitor/enable (true|false)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { load_monitor_enable: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/loadMonitor/measuredImpedance (-?[\d.]+)$'
    throttle: 0.5
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { impedance: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/loadMonitor/highLimit (-?[\d.]+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { load_high_limit: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/loadMonitor/lowLimit (-?[\d.]+)$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { load_low_limit: $2 } }
  - match: '^/amp/channels/(\d+)/loadMonitor/status "(.*)"$'
    child_set:
      - { type: channel, id: $1, state: { load_status: $2 } }

  # ── Analog inputs ──
  - match: '^/amp/inputs/analog/(\d+)/sensitivity "(.*)"$'
    child_set:
      - { type: analog_input, id: $1, state: { sensitivity: $2 } }

  # ── Device info ──
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/deviceName "(.*)"$'
    set: { device_name: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/venueName "(.*)"$'
    set: { venue_name: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/modelID "(.*)"$'
    set: { model_id: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/assetTagNumber "(.*)"$'
    set: { asset_tag: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/installerName "(.*)"$'
    set: { installer_name: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/installerContactInfo "(.*)"$'
    set: { installer_contact: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/dateOfInstallation "(.*)"$'
    set: { date_of_installation: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/rackName "(.*)"$'
    set: { rack_name: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/rackPosition "(.*)"$'
    set: { rack_position: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/serialNumber "(.*)"$'
    set: { serial_number: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/dateOfMfg "(.*)"$'
    set: { date_of_mfg: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/hardwareID "(.*)"$'
    set: { hardware_id: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/firmwareVersion "(.*)"$'
    set: { firmware_version: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/powerSupplyfirmwareVersion "(.*)"$'
    set: { psu_firmware_version: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/amp12firmwareVersion "(.*)"$'
    set: { amp12_firmware_version: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/amp34firmwareVersion "(.*)"$'
    set: { amp34_firmware_version: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/upTime "(.*)"$'
    set: { uptime: "$1" }
  # numInputs / numOutputs come back as floats ("4.0"); capture the whole part
  # so the integer coercion doesn't choke on the decimal.
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/numInputs (\d+)(?:\.\d+)?$'
    set: { num_inputs: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/deviceInfo/numOutputs (\d+)(?:\.\d+)?$'
    set: { num_outputs: "$1" }

  # ── Power supply ──
  # AC readings push live (subscribed unconditionally); throttle just above the
  # amp's measured push rate so a busy reading can't flood, without dropping the
  # live update.
  - match: '^/amp/powerSupply/acLineVoltage (-?[\d.]+)$'
    throttle: 0.5
    set: { ac_line_voltage: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/powerSupply/acLineCurrent (-?[\d.]+)$'
    throttle: 0.5
    set: { ac_line_current: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/powerSupply/acLineWatts (-?[\d.]+)$'
    throttle: 0.5
    set: { ac_line_watts: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/powerSupply/fault (true|false)$'
    set: { psu_fault: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/powerSupply/thermal (true|false)$'
    set: { psu_thermal: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/powerSupply/powerOk (true|false)$'
    set: { psu_power_ok: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/powerSupply/lineWarning (true|false)$'
    set: { psu_line_warning: "$1" }

  # ── Auto standby / signal generator ──
  - match: '^/amp/autoStandby/enable (true|false)$'
    set: { auto_standby_enable: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/autoStandby/threshold (-?[\d.]+)$'
    set: { auto_standby_threshold: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/autoStandby/timeToWait (\d+)(?:\.\d+)?$'
    set: { auto_standby_wait: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/signalGenerator/type "(.*)"$'
    set: { signal_gen_type: "$1" }
  - match: '^/amp/signalGenerator/frequency (\d+)(?:\.\d+)?$'
    set: { signal_gen_frequency: "$1" }

  # ── Errors ──
  # e.g. error: unsupported value: Post Toasties (/amp/.../danteOnRamp)
  - match: '^(error: .+)$'
    set: { last_error: "$1" }

on_connect:
  # Subscribe to the whole surface. The subscribe reply carries the element's
  # current value, so this doubles as the initial state sync — no separate
  # "get everything" pass. The amp then reports every change on this same
  # connection, including changes made from its own web UI.

  # ── Device identity + status ──
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/deviceName\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/venueName\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/modelID\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/assetTagNumber\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/installerName\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/installerContactInfo\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/dateOfInstallation\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/rackName\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/rackPosition\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/serialNumber\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/dateOfMfg\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/hardwareID\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/firmwareVersion\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/powerSupplyfirmwareVersion\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/amp12firmwareVersion\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/amp34firmwareVersion\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/upTime\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/numInputs\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/deviceInfo/numOutputs\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/powerSupply/fault\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/powerSupply/thermal\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/powerSupply/powerOk\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/powerSupply/lineWarning\n"
  # AC power readings are amp-health telemetry, not an audio meter, so they push
  # live always (not gated behind Enable Level Meters). Low-rate and always
  # welcome — a static power number reads as a dead device.
  - "subscribe /amp/powerSupply/acLineVoltage\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/powerSupply/acLineCurrent\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/powerSupply/acLineWatts\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/autoStandby/enable\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/autoStandby/threshold\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/autoStandby/timeToWait\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/signalGenerator/type\n"
  - "subscribe /amp/signalGenerator/frequency\n"

  # ── Per channel: output ──
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/output/name\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/output/enable\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/output/mute\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/output/fader\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/output/hiZLoZ\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/output/hiZHpfFrequency\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/output/fault\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/output/thermal\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/output/limiting\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/output/clip\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/output/signalDetect\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/output/ready\n" }

  # ── Per channel: input selector ──
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/primary\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/primaryFader\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/primarySignalDetect\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/primaryClip\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/primaryThreshold\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/secondary\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/secondaryFader\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/secondarySignalDetect\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/secondaryClip\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/secondaryThreshold\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/signalDetect\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/clip\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/mode\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/signalGeneratorEnable\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/signalGeneratorFader\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/danteOnRamp\n" }

  # ── Per channel: crossover ──
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/crossover/bandGainAndDelay/gain\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/crossover/bandGainAndDelay/delay\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/crossover/bandGainAndDelay/invert\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/crossover/lowPassFilter/enable\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/crossover/lowPassFilter/type\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/crossover/lowPassFilter/frequency\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/crossover/highPassFilter/enable\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/crossover/highPassFilter/type\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/crossover/highPassFilter/frequency\n" }

  # ── Per channel: limiters + load monitor ──
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/rmsLimiter/enable\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/rmsLimiter/threshold\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/rmsLimiter/attackTime\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/rmsLimiter/releaseTime\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/peakLimiter/enable\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/peakLimiter/threshold\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/peakLimiter/attackTime\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/peakLimiter/releaseTime\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/loadMonitor/enable\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/loadMonitor/measuredImpedance\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/loadMonitor/highLimit\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/loadMonitor/lowLimit\n" }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/loadMonitor/status\n" }

  # ── Per analog input ──
  - { each_child: analog_input, send: "subscribe /amp/inputs/analog/{child_id}/sensitivity\n" }

  # ── Meters: only when the integrator asked for them ──
  # These are the elements the amp streams continuously.
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/levels/level_db\n", when: enable_meters }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/levels/level_volts\n", when: enable_meters }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/levels/level_watts\n", when: enable_meters }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/primaryLevel\n", when: enable_meters }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/inputSelector/secondaryLevel\n", when: enable_meters }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/rmsLimiter/gainReduction\n", when: enable_meters }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/rmsLimiter/totalGainReduction\n", when: enable_meters }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/peakLimiter/gainReduction\n", when: enable_meters }
  - { each_child: channel, send: "subscribe /amp/channels/{child_id}/peakLimiter/totalGainReduction\n", when: enable_meters }
  # (AC line V/A/W are subscribed unconditionally above — not meter-gated.)

polling:
  # Everything else arrives by subscription, so this loop exists only to refresh
  # the per-channel output level/volts/watts while Enable Level Meters is OFF —
  # a slow read that keeps output telemetry roughly current without a live meter.
  # With meters ON these reads are redundant but harmless (the subscription is
  # already fresher). AC power is not here — it is subscribed unconditionally, so
  # it pushes live in both states.
  queries:
    - { each_child: channel, send: "get /amp/channels/{child_id}/levels/level_db\n" }
    - { each_child: channel, send: "get /amp/channels/{child_id}/levels/level_volts\n" }
    - { each_child: channel, send: "get /amp/channels/{child_id}/levels/level_watts\n" }

liveness:
  # This driver is push-mostly: with meters off and a long poll interval, the
  # amp can go quiet for minutes at a time, and a unit that vanishes without a
  # FIN would otherwise sit "connected" until the OS keepalive noticed. A cheap
  # element read proves the API is still answering.
  send: "get /amp/deviceInfo/firmwareVersion\n"
  expect: '/amp/deviceInfo/firmwareVersion'
  interval: 30
  timeout: 5
  max_failures: 2

simulator:
  # The LEA grammar is get/set/subscribe/unsubscribe over a flat element tree,
  # which the auto-generated per-command handlers can't model (they only match
  # exact command strings). One dispatcher handler owns the whole protocol
  # instead: it parses the verb, validates the element against the real element
  # map, tracks subscriptions, and clamps out-of-range numbers the way the amp
  # does. It mirrors firmware 3.1.7.0 as verified on a Connect 352D: a successful
  # set is SILENT (no "OK"), the only reply being the change notice pushed to a
  # subscriber; a bad enum/bool value is dropped silently; a bad number or an
  # unknown element gets the amp's real "error:  ..." string (two spaces); and
  # every numeric renders as a float ("70.0"), even conceptual integers.
  command_handlers:
    - match: '(?s:.+)'
      handler: |
        def _run():
            line = match.group(0).strip()
            if not line:
                return

            # Element map: suffix -> (kind, default). kind drives value parsing
            # and the reply's quoting, exactly as the amp does it.
            #   b = boolean (bare true/false), n = number, i = integer,
            #   s = string/enum (double-quoted)
            AMP = {
                "/amp/deviceInfo/deviceName": ("s", "Connect 704D"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/venueName": ("s", "LEA Office"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/modelID": ("s", "Connect Series Model 704D"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/assetTagNumber": ("s", "BJD-704D-0001"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/installerName": ("s", "Acme AV"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/installerContactInfo": ("s", "1-800-123-4567"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/dateOfInstallation": ("s", "2020-02-16T20:47:00.000Z"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/rackName": ("s", "Rack 1"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/rackPosition": ("s", "RU 1"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/serialNumber": ("s", "31890067"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/dateOfMfg": ("s", "191115041907"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/hardwareID": ("s", "2"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/firmwareVersion": ("s", "2.0.1.11"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/powerSupplyfirmwareVersion": ("s", "1.0.3.3"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/amp12firmwareVersion": ("s", "1.0.3.1"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/amp34firmwareVersion": ("s", "1.0.3.1"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/upTime": ("s", "N/A"),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/numInputs": ("f", 4.0),
                "/amp/deviceInfo/numOutputs": ("f", 4.0),
                "/amp/powerSupply/acLineVoltage": ("n", 118.0),
                "/amp/powerSupply/acLineCurrent": ("n", 0.5),
                "/amp/powerSupply/acLineWatts": ("n", 58.0),
                "/amp/powerSupply/fault": ("b", False),
                "/amp/powerSupply/thermal": ("b", False),
                "/amp/powerSupply/powerOk": ("b", True),
                "/amp/powerSupply/lineWarning": ("b", True),
                "/amp/autoStandby/enable": ("b", False),
                "/amp/autoStandby/threshold": ("n", -60.0),
                "/amp/autoStandby/timeToWait": ("i", 15),
                "/amp/signalGenerator/type": ("s", "Pink Noise"),
                "/amp/signalGenerator/frequency": ("i", 1000),
            }
            # Per-channel elements (suffix after /amp/channels/<n>).
            CH = {
                "/output/name": ("s", "Channel"),
                "/output/enable": ("b", True),
                "/output/mute": ("b", False),
                "/output/fader": ("n", 0.0),
                "/output/hiZLoZ": ("s", "LoZ"),
                "/output/hiZHpfFrequency": ("i", 70),
                "/output/fault": ("b", False),
                "/output/thermal": ("b", False),
                "/output/limiting": ("b", False),
                "/output/clip": ("b", False),
                "/output/signalDetect": ("b", False),
                "/output/ready": ("b", True),
                "/levels/level_db": ("n", -52.78131103515625),
                "/levels/level_volts": ("n", 24.5),
                "/levels/level_watts": ("n", 85.5),
                "/inputSelector/primary": ("s", "Analog 1"),
                "/inputSelector/primaryFader": ("n", 0.0),
                "/inputSelector/primaryLevel": ("n", -52.2),
                "/inputSelector/primarySignalDetect": ("b", True),
                "/inputSelector/primaryClip": ("b", False),
                "/inputSelector/primaryThreshold": ("n", -60.0),
                "/inputSelector/secondary": ("s", "None"),
                "/inputSelector/secondaryFader": ("n", 0.0),
                "/inputSelector/secondaryLevel": ("n", -80.0),
                "/inputSelector/secondarySignalDetect": ("b", False),
                "/inputSelector/secondaryClip": ("b", False),
                "/inputSelector/secondaryThreshold": ("n", -55.0),
                "/inputSelector/signalDetect": ("b", True),
                "/inputSelector/clip": ("b", False),
                "/inputSelector/mode": ("s", "Backup"),
                "/inputSelector/signalGeneratorEnable": ("b", False),
                "/inputSelector/signalGeneratorFader": ("n", -20.0),
                "/inputSelector/danteOnRamp": ("s", "Analog Input"),
                "/crossover/bandGainAndDelay/gain": ("n", 0.0),
                "/crossover/bandGainAndDelay/delay": ("n", 0.0),
                "/crossover/bandGainAndDelay/invert": ("b", False),
                "/crossover/lowPassFilter/enable": ("b", False),
                "/crossover/lowPassFilter/type": ("s", "Butterworth 12dB/oct"),
                "/crossover/lowPassFilter/frequency": ("i", 20000),
                "/crossover/highPassFilter/enable": ("b", True),
                "/crossover/highPassFilter/type": ("s", "Butterworth 12dB/oct"),
                "/crossover/highPassFilter/frequency": ("i", 70),
                "/rmsLimiter/enable": ("b", True),
                "/rmsLimiter/threshold": ("n", 70.0),
                "/rmsLimiter/attackTime": ("n", 1000.0),
                "/rmsLimiter/releaseTime": ("n", 10000.0),
                "/rmsLimiter/gainReduction": ("n", 0.0),
                "/rmsLimiter/totalGainReduction": ("n", 0.0),
                "/peakLimiter/enable": ("b", True),
                "/peakLimiter/threshold": ("n", 141.0),
                "/peakLimiter/attackTime": ("n", 10.0),
                "/peakLimiter/releaseTime": ("n", 128.0),
                "/peakLimiter/gainReduction": ("n", 0.0),
                "/peakLimiter/totalGainReduction": ("n", 0.0),
                "/loadMonitor/enable": ("b", True),
                "/loadMonitor/measuredImpedance": ("n", 8.2),
                "/loadMonitor/highLimit": ("n", 48.0),
                "/loadMonitor/lowLimit": ("n", 2.5),
                "/loadMonitor/status": ("s", "Ok"),
            }
            EQ = {
                "/enable": ("b", False),
                "/type": ("s", "Parametric"),
                "/gain": ("n", 0.0),
                "/frequency": ("i", 1000),
                "/q": ("n", 4.0),
            }
            # Ranges the amp clamps to (out-of-range is clamped, never refused).
            LIMITS = {
                "/output/fader": (-80.0, 0.0),
                "/output/hiZHpfFrequency": (35, 5000),
                "/inputSelector/primaryFader": (-80.0, 0.0),
                "/inputSelector/secondaryFader": (-80.0, 0.0),
                "/inputSelector/primaryThreshold": (-80.0, 0.0),
                "/inputSelector/secondaryThreshold": (-80.0, 0.0),
                "/inputSelector/signalGeneratorFader": (-80.0, 0.0),
                "/crossover/bandGainAndDelay/gain": (-15.0, 15.0),
                "/crossover/bandGainAndDelay/delay": (0.0, 100.0),
                "/crossover/lowPassFilter/frequency": (20, 20000),
                "/crossover/highPassFilter/frequency": (20, 20000),
                "/rmsLimiter/threshold": (10.0, 140.0),
                "/rmsLimiter/attackTime": (1000.0, 10000.0),
                "/rmsLimiter/releaseTime": (1000.0, 10000.0),
                "/peakLimiter/threshold": (14.0, 198.0),
                "/peakLimiter/attackTime": (1.0, 1000.0),
                "/peakLimiter/releaseTime": (1.0, 1000.0),
                "/loadMonitor/highLimit": (8.0, 250.0),
                "/loadMonitor/lowLimit": (1.0, 250.0),
                "/amp/autoStandby/threshold": (-80.0, 0.0),
                "/amp/autoStandby/timeToWait": (1, 240),
                "/amp/signalGenerator/frequency": (20, 20000),
            }
            # Enum values the amp validates (an unlisted value is an error).
            ENUMS = {
                "/output/hiZLoZ": ["HiZ-70V", "HiZ-100V", "LoZ"],
                "/inputSelector/mode": ["Override", "Backup"],
                "/inputSelector/danteOnRamp": ["Analog Input", "Post Crossover"],
                "/loadMonitor/status": ["Ok", "Short", "Open", "Low Signal"],
                "/amp/signalGenerator/type": ["Pink Noise", "White Noise", "Tone"],
            }
            SOURCES = ["None"]
            for _fam in ("Analog", "Dante"):
                for _n in (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8):
                    SOURCES.append(_fam + " " + str(_n))
                for _p in ("1+2", "3+4", "5+6", "7+8"):
                    SOURCES.append(_fam + " " + _p)
            ENUMS["/inputSelector/primary"] = SOURCES
            ENUMS["/inputSelector/secondary"] = SOURCES
            FILTERS = [
                "Butterworth 6dB/oct", "Butterworth 12dB/oct",
                "Butterworth 18dB/oct", "Butterworth 24dB/oct",
                "Butterworth 48dB/oct", "Linkwitz-Riley 24dB/oct",
                "Linkwitz-Riley 48dB/oct", "Bessel 6dB/oct",
                "Bessel 12dB/oct", "Bessel 18dB/oct",
                "Bessel 24dB/oct", "Bessel 48dB/oct",
            ]
            ENUMS["/crossover/lowPassFilter/type"] = FILTERS
            ENUMS["/crossover/highPassFilter/type"] = FILTERS

            CHANNELS = 4
            INPUTS = 4
            EQ_BANDS = 8

            def spec(url):
                """(kind, default, limit_key) for a URL, or None if the amp has
                no such element."""
                if url in AMP:
                    k, d = AMP[url]
                    return k, d, url
                m = re.match(r"^/amp/channels/(\d+)(/.+)$", url)
                if m:
                    ch = int(m.group(1))
                    if ch < 1 or ch > CHANNELS:
                        return None
                    rest = m.group(2)
                    if rest in CH:
                        k, d = CH[rest]
                        if rest == "/output/name":
                            d = "Channel " + str(ch)
                        return k, d, rest
                    eq = re.match(r"^/outputEqFilters/(\d+)(/.+)$", rest)
                    if eq and 1 <= int(eq.group(1)) <= EQ_BANDS and eq.group(2) in EQ:
                        k, d = EQ[eq.group(2)]
                        return k, d, eq.group(2)
                    return None
                m = re.match(r"^/amp/inputs/analog/(\d+)/sensitivity$", url)
                if m and 1 <= int(m.group(1)) <= INPUTS:
                    return "s", "26dB", "/sensitivity"
                return None

            def current(url, kind, default):
                val = state.get(url)
                return default if val is None else val

            def render(url, kind, value):
                """Format an element's value the way the amp reports it. Every
                numeric comes back as a float on real firmware — even conceptual
                integers (numOutputs "2.0", a frequency "1000.0")."""
                if kind == "b":
                    return url + " " + ("true" if value else "false")
                if kind == "s":
                    return url + ' "' + str(value) + '"'
                if kind in ("f", "i"):
                    return url + " " + format(float(value), ".1f")
                return url + " " + str(float(value))

            parts = line.split(None, 2)
            verb = parts[0].lower()
            # An unrecognized verb (or a bare word) is a parse error. Note the two
            # spaces after 'error:' — that is what firmware 3.1.7.0 emits.
            if verb not in ("get", "set", "subscribe", "unsubscribe") or len(parts) < 2:
                respond("error:  cannot parse - '" + line + "'")
                return
            url = parts[1]
            found = spec(url)
            if not found:
                # A well-formed /amp/ path that doesn't resolve is
                # "object/element does not exist"; anything else is "cannot parse".
                if url.startswith("/amp/"):
                    respond("error:  object/element does not exist - '" + url + "'")
                else:
                    respond("error:  cannot parse - '" + line + "'")
                return
            kind, default, lkey = found

            if verb == "get":
                respond(render(url, kind, current(url, kind, default)))
                return

            if verb == "subscribe":
                subs = state.get("_subs") or ""
                if url not in subs.split("|"):
                    state["_subs"] = (subs + "|" + url) if subs else url
                respond(render(url, kind, current(url, kind, default)))
                return

            if verb == "unsubscribe":
                subs = [s for s in (state.get("_subs") or "").split("|") if s and s != url]
                state["_subs"] = "|".join(subs)
                respond("OK")
                return

            # set — a missing value is a parse error.
            if len(parts) < 3:
                respond("error:  cannot parse - '" + line + "'")
                return
            raw = parts[2].strip()
            if raw.startswith('"') and raw.endswith('"') and len(raw) >= 2:
                raw = raw[1:-1]

            if kind == "b":
                # A bool takes only true/false; any other value is dropped
                # SILENTLY (no error, no change) on current firmware.
                if raw.lower() not in ("true", "false"):
                    return
                value = raw.lower() == "true"
            elif kind == "s":
                # An enum with an unsupported value is dropped SILENTLY too; a
                # free string (no ENUMS entry) accepts anything.
                allowed = ENUMS.get(lkey)
                if allowed is not None and raw not in allowed:
                    return
                value = raw
            else:
                # A non-numeric value for a numeric element IS a loud parse error;
                # an out-of-range number is clamped, not refused.
                try:
                    num = float(raw)
                except (TypeError, ValueError):
                    respond("error:  cannot parse - '" + line + "'")
                    return
                lim = LIMITS.get(lkey)
                if lim:
                    num = min(max(num, float(lim[0])), float(lim[1]))
                value = int(num) if kind in ("i", "f") else num

            # A successful set is SILENT on current firmware — no OK. The only
            # reply is the change notice, and only to a subscriber, and only when
            # the value actually changed (setting a value to itself is silent).
            old = current(url, kind, default)
            state[url] = value
            subs = (state.get("_subs") or "").split("|")
            if url in subs and value != old:
                respond(render(url, kind, value))

        _run()
